#!/usr/bin/env -S ping-bulk -f
# Full-featured example showing sections, brace expansion, static DNS
# overrides, :for loops, and SSH-based remote monitoring.
#
# Run directly:  chmod +x network.hosts && ./network.hosts
# Or:            ping-bulk -f network.hosts

# ── Static DNS overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Map IP ranges to meaningful names.
# Back-references (all equivalent): \N  \{N}  $N  ${N}  (N = 1 for first brace group)
# \0 / $0 expands to the full expanded host string for each iteration.
:resolv 10.0.0.1      gw-core
:resolv 10.0.1.{1..4} leaf-sw$1
:resolv 10.0.2.{1..8} server${1}

# ── Display preferences (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
:set stats down
:set ping-view scaled
:set dns hostname

## Core
10.0.0.1

## Distribution switches
10.0.1.{1..4}

## Servers
10.0.2.{1..8}

## Public DNS (for connectivity check)
8.8.8.8
1.1.1.1

# ── For-loop: two brace groups → two back-references ──────────────────────
# $1 = rack number (first group),  $2 = node number (second group)
# Generates 6 entries: 10.3.1.1, 10.3.1.2, 10.3.2.1, 10.3.2.2, 10.3.3.1, 10.3.3.2
## Pod servers
:for 10.3.{1..3}.{1..2}
:resolv $0 rack$1-node$2
$0
:done

# ── Remote monitoring over SSH ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ping hosts on a remote network segment as seen from a remote server.
# Requires passwordless SSH access (key or agent).

:title Remote site A (via ssh jump)
:ssh-begin -J bastion.example.com ops@remote-a
10.10.0.{1..4}
:ssh-end

:title Remote site B
:ssh ops@remote-b 10.20.0.1
:ssh ops@remote-b 10.20.0.{2..5}

